< https://github.com/tacplus-dev/gateway/issues/34#issuecomment-6854292613 Blocked-by: tacplus-dev/cluster#18 Blocked-by: #35
Issue #34 isn't finished: the fix is committed and queued to land, but nothing has merged and no `v0.1.2` tag exists yet. I've marked the issue as blocked.

**The fix:** the build image's node 26 removed `--experimental-transform-types`. So the flag wasn't too new for the pinned image, as the issue guessed; it was already gone. webapp-login now uses only TypeScript that node can run by stripping the types: constructor parameter properties are written as ordinary fields, and `tsconfig.json` sets `erasableSyntaxOnly` so `tsc` rejects anything else. `npm test` is now `tsc && node --test test/*.test.ts`, with no flag.

- **Commits** on `looper/gateway-34`, rebased on main 600215d: `4fbecf3` (the fix) and `8bc28f5` (STATE.md).
- **Tested:** only `npm test` here on node 24, where all 23 tests pass. I have no container runtime, so `just gates` has not run in the build image.
- **Land:** queued at 13:16Z. No runner has picked up its build: the status has been `pending` since 12:53Z. The previous two lands ended the same way, with "no verdict within 3h", not a test failure.

**Why it waits:**
- tacplus-dev/cluster#18: there are no runners for build jobs.
- gateway#35: clippy fails on main, so a full gates run would be red even with a runner.

I wrote both as `Blocked-by` lines to the outcome file and posted this status on the issue.

The failure on unchanged main in the build image is still not confirmed, because its build also got no verdict. Once the land goes green, the next run tags `v0.1.2`, comments and closes the issue. There are no release branches, so nothing needs backporting. No service handlers were touched, so the trace check didn't apply.
